 release).

Package: libnss-nostr
Section: admin
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: NSS module projecting the nostr identity authority into passwd/group
 libnss-nostr installs the read-only glibc NSS module libnss_nostr.so.2
 which projects nostr-authd's identity authority (a SQLite projection
 written atomically by the broker) into passwd/group lookups. Admins wire
 it into /etc/nsswitch.conf; the module reads its configuration from
 /etc/nss_nostr.conf.
 .
 Install nostr-login for the full broker+PAM+NSS login stack.

Package: libpam-nostr
Section: admin
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         libpam-runtime (>= 1.0.1-6),
         nostr-authd (>= ${source:Version})
Recommends: libnss-nostr (>= ${source:Version})
Description: PAM module authenticating against the nostr auth broker
 libpam-nostr installs pam_nostr.so, the broker-backed PAM authenticator
 that consults nostr-authd via /run/nostr-auth/auth.sock. It also ships
 the pam-auth-update profile /usr/share/pam-configs/nostr so admins can
 compose pam_nostr into common-auth / common-account with
 `pam-auth-update --package` rather than editing gdm-password or
 common-auth by hand.
 .
 Semantics are the strict-deny posture (beads nostrc-o1ho): known nostr
 accounts with a failed proof are refused (default=die), unknown accounts
 fall through to Unix auth (user_unknown=ignore), and a stopped broker
 never bricks local login (authinfo_unavail=ignore).

Package: nostr-authd
Section: admin
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Nostr authentication broker daemon
 nostr-authd is the SOCK_SEQPACKET broker that mediates authentication for
 the nostr-homed login stack. It vends CHECK_ACCOUNT / BEGIN_LOGIN /
 SUBMIT_PROOF over the privileged /run/nostr-auth/auth.sock, backs a
 local-vault provider (encrypted authority.db) and a NIP-46 external
 signer provider, and re-publishes a read-only NSS projection consumed by
 libnss_nostr.so.2.
 .
 Ships a hardened systemd unit
 (RuntimeDirectory=nostr-auth/0711, StateDirectory=nostr-auth/0700,
 ProtectSystem=strict, RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_UNIX,
 MemoryDenyWriteExecute=yes) and the /etc/nostr-auth/auth.conf conffile.

Package: nostr-homectl
Section: admin
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, nostr-authd (>= ${source:Version})
Description: Headless identity-authority admin CLI for nostr-homed
 nostr-homectl is the GLib-free / FUSE-free identity-authority admin CLI
 (NOSTR_HOMED_ENABLE_CTL, decision D-11). It queries and mutates the
 authority store owned by nostr-authd -- listing accounts, exporting the
 read-only NSS projection, and driving disable/enable transitions.
 .
 Also ships nostr-homed-seed (the provisioning tool renamed from
 nh-seed-authority) in /usr/sbin, which mints the encrypted vault and
 the NSS projection for new accounts.

Package: nostr-homed-smb
Section: admin
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         cifs-utils,
         nostr-authd (>= ${source:Version})
Recommends: samba-common-bin
Suggests: gvfs-backends
Description: SMB credential acquisition tools for nostr-homed
 nostr-smb-acquire drives BEGIN_SMB_PROOF against nostr-authd's
 /run/nostr-auth/user.sock and delivers the minted, short-lived SMB
 password as a Samba credentials= file (mode 0600) or, with --stdout,
 to a one-shot pipe. nostr-smb-mount is the shell wrapper that consumes
 that credentials file and mounts the share via mount.cifs (default) or
 gvfs (--mode gvfs).
 .
 Install this together with nostr-login for a headless server that
 authenticates SMB shares through the nostr broker.

Package: nostr-homed-domain
Section: admin
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3
Description: Inert winbind / Samba AD domain samples for nostr-homed
 Ships the winbind and Samba AD configuration samples used by nostr-homed
 to document a domain-joined deployment, plus the
 validate_domain_profile.py profile validator. Nothing in this package
 activates PAM or winbind -- it is inert by design and is safe to install
 on a stock host.

Package: nostr-login
Section: metapackages
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         libnss-nostr (>= ${source:Version}),
         libpam-nostr (>= ${source:Version}),
         nostr-authd (>= ${source:Version}),
         nostr-homectl (>= ${source:Version})
Recommends: nostr-homed-smb (>= ${source:Version})
Suggests: nostr-homed-domain (>= ${source:Version})
Description: Headless nostr login stack (metapackage)
 Depends on the four components that make up a working nostr login stack
 on a headless server: the NSS projection (libnss-nostr), the broker-backed
 PAM module (libpam-nostr), the auth broker daemon (nostr-authd) and the
 identity-authority admin CLI (nostr-homectl).
 .
 The dependency closure is deliberately headless (decision D-14): no
 GTK/GNOME/gvfs/libsecret/libpeas/webkit/gstreamer/FUSE, and no GLib.
